Contrariwise, maybe the issue is that the game is
being _way_ too hasty to put up that DYWYPI when the
player has "died" as a troll?

Regular game trolls, after all, by being "merely
dead" aren't yet "really quite sincerely" dead, much
like the hero in The Princess Bride.

Instead, time could be run for the monsters to loot
the corpse, lose interest, and wander off noshing
happily on adventurer provinder and tripe rations,
and practicing with their newly stolen artifacts,
until the corpse either revives, leaving a quite
chastened adventurer, or rots, leaving a ghost
presiding over a bones pile much diminished, to only
crud not even a monster finds worth carrying away,
and a bones level, if any, full of monsters
carrying or wearing all the good stuff.

This would make playing polymorphed into a troll a
great game abuse, much like having a built-in amulet
of "probabilistic life-saving (and charge a bundle
for the privilege)".

It seems only fair that playing as a troll gets
_all_ of that monster's special abilities, just
like playing as other monsters does.

Since watching the crowd disperse would be an
interesting feature in any case, maybe all but the
reviving aspect could be extended to other player
types as well, with a new #die command to hasten
the process to its conclusion?

